Supervisor run complete.

## What the escalation actually was

`C8_issues broken` was the trigger, not a code bug — 12 issues flagged for triage. Only **#28** was a real defect; I verified rather than assumed.

## Issue #28 — COMEBin marker-seed crash (real bug, fixed)

Root cause: `test_getmarker_2quarter.pl` uses exit codes **2/3/4** to mean "no usable seed set". `gen_seed()` treated every non-zero status as a tool failure, escalating an ordinary *empty result* into `RuntimeError`, which then killed the run with `Clustering exited with status 1`.

Commit `41606c8` on `comebin-optimizations-v11` (in the COMEBin repo, not the benchmark repo — so it never collided with the concurrent agent):
- `MARKER_NO_SEED_EXIT_CODES = {2,3,4}` + `allowed_returncodes` on `_run_external_command`
- `gen_seed()` warns, publishes no seed file, returns `0`; `bin`/`get_result` short-circuit to "Reporting 0 bins", exit `0`
- Genuine failures (status 1, or outside 2/3/4) **still raise** — breakage isn't silenced

Verification: 5/5 new regression tests pass (the same test on the parent commit gives 10 failures including the exact reported traceback); the reported signature reproduced on real data now exits 0.

**The important part — the 0-bins scare was a false alarm.** A regression run of mine reported `exit_code: 1 / 0 bins`, and I did not blame or absolve the patch without evidence. An A/B against the pre-patch commit on byte-identical inputs gave: marker seed byte-identical, **121/121 Leiden grids bit-identical**, winning labels identical. Both commits produce 0 bins because that fixture is 3.5 Mbp total and no cluster reaches `MINIMUM_FINAL_BIN_SIZE` (200 kb) — largest is 124 kb. Pre-existing, unrelated to the fix; larger fixtures are unaffected (CAMI III = 492 bins).

## Deploy drift (both directions)

- `supervise-alive.sh` was a **live 5-min cron job with no repo source** — unversioned, and no future edit could ever reach it. Added to source control.
- Added check **`C1c_unsourced_bin`**, because `C1b` only walks repo→bin and was structurally blind to exactly this. It reports `degraded` rather than auto-fixing — adding a source is a judgement call, not a mechanical repair.

## Deliberate non-actions

- **No `.issues_done` markers** — no issue is verified complete. Closed nothing by any other means.
- **#27 got no comment** — the agent had already answered it accurately at 12:52:42Z; posting would have been a duplicate.
- **Did not run `benchmark-watchdog.sh`** to clear the stale `.active_run` pointers — it would have relaunched a multi-hour full baseline. I verified both pids dead and removed the pointers directly.
- Left the `pymp-*` `Errno 16` tracebacks alone (non-fatal, epoch 200 reached) to keep blast radius small; noted on #28.

## Commits

| repo | commit | note |
|---|---|---|
| COMEBin-v11 | `41606c8` | local only — **not yet on GitHub** |
| benchmark | `96aaa1b9` | 2 paths exactly, pushed to `main` |

Benchmark push held `/tmp/bench-repo.lock`, hard-guarded the staged set, verified the index was empty first, and fast-forwarded over the agent's `b6f1fd6f` so their in-flight work (README, plots, run tables) was preserved untouched.

**Final:** C1b ok · C1c ok · bin↔repo exact · HEAD=origin/main · worktree clean · no active run · 315 GiB free · 1/3 escalations.

⚠️ **One thing needs the agent:** `41606c8` is still local-only (`origin/comebin-optimizations-v11` is at `95f5ea8`). The merge to `master` and bioconda release you asked for on #28 is **not done** — I flagged this explicitly in the issue comment so it isn't lost. Master is now a clean 2-commit fast-forward with no divergence, so it's a clean merge whenever the agent picks it up.

