s.\n2026-09-25 19:33:08,276 - Marker seed generation command: /usr/local/bin/perl /usr/local/bin/auxiliary/test_getmarker_2quarter.pl /data/jwd06/main/000/113/398/113398681/working/ERR9966616.fasta.bacar_marker.hmmout /data/jwd06/main/000/113/398/113398681/working/ERR9966616.fasta 1001 /data/jwd06/main/000/113/398/113398681/working/.ERR9966616.fasta.bacar_marker.2quarter_lencutoff_1001.seed.28193.xdu5qe1_.tmp\n2026-09-25 19:33:09,622 - Marker seed generation exited with status 3; stderr=/data/jwd06/main/000/113/398/113398681/working/ERR9966616.fasta.bacar_marker.2quarter_lencutoff_1001.seed.err.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/usr/local/bin/COMEBin/main.py\", line 381, in <module>\n    main()\n    ~~~~^^\n  File \"/usr/local/bin/COMEBin/main.py\", line 298, in main\n    _ = gen_seed(logger, args.contig_file, num_threads, args.contig_len, marker_name=\"bacar_marker\",\n                 quarter=\"2quarter\", hmm_evalue=args.hmm_evalue)\n  File \"/usr/local/bin/COMEBin/utils.py\", line 307, in gen_seed\n    _run_external_command(\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\n        logger, 'Marker seed generation',\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n        [perl_executable, marker_script, hmm_result, contig_file, contig_length_threshold, seed_temp],\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n        str(seed_result) + '.out', str(seed_result) + '.err')\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/bin/COMEBin/utils.py\", line 188, in _run_external_command\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"{label} failed with status {completed.returncode}; stderr={stderr_path}{detail}\")\nRuntimeError: Marker seed generation failed with status 3; stderr=/data/jwd06/main/000/113/398/113398681/working/ERR9966616.fasta.bacar_marker.2quarter_lencutoff_1001.seed.err; tail=Marker hits mapped to input contigs, but no usable marker seed set could be generated.\nClustering exited with status 1.\n```\n\nCan you fix it, a valid fix would also to report no bins but do not error out, I want this fix with the other updates tested on the benchark data, then merged in the master branch ready to release in bioconda","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXed4yQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Fixed on `comebin-optimizations-v11` @ **`41606c8`** — COMEBin now reports **0 bins and exits 0** instead of raising, and the pipeline no longer dies with `Clustering exited with status 1`.\n\n### Root cause\n`auxiliary/test_getmarker_2quarter.pl` uses distinct exit codes to say \"I could not build a usable seed set\": `2` (no marker hit matches a contig), `3` (hits mapped, but no gene passes the completeness/coverage gate), `4` (no marker hits at all). `gen_seed()` treated every non-zero status as a hard tool failure, so a perfectly ordinary *empty result* — your case, `status 3` — was escalated to `RuntimeError: Marker seed generation failed with status 3`.\n\n### The fix\n- `COMEBin/utils.py`: new `MARKER_NO_SEED_EXIT_CODES = frozenset({2, 3, 4})`; `_run_external_command()` takes an `allowed_returncodes` argument so an expected empty outcome is not conflated with a genuine crash.\n- `gen_seed()` logs a clear warning, publishes **no** seed file, and returns `0`.\n- `COMEBin/main.py`: `bin` and `get_result` short-circuit when `seed_count == 0` and exit `0` with an explicit `Reporting 0 bins ... This is an empty result for this input, not an error.`\n- A real tool failure (status 1, or any code outside 2/3/4) still raises, so genuine breakage is not silenced.\n\n### Verification\n1. **New regression test** `tests/test_marker_seed_empty_result.py` — 5 cases (statuses 2/3/4, plus the happy path through `main.py bin` and `get_result`): **all pass**. Run against the parent commit `95f5ea8` the same test reports 10 failures, including your exact traceback (`utils.py` line 188 in `_run_external_command`, rc=1) — so the test genuinely pins the bug.\n2. **Your signature, on real data** — 300-contig assembly with 208 real HMM hits reproduces `status 3` + `tail=Marker hits mapped to input contigs, but no usable marker seed set could be generated.`; it now exits `0` with `Reporting 0 bins`.\n3. **No regression on the happy path, on benchmark data** — full small-dataset benchmark run (`run_small_test.sh`, seed 42, 200 epochs, 121 Leiden grids), patched `41606c8` vs pre-patch `95f5ea8`, same byte-identical inputs:\n   - marker seed file: **byte-identical** to the known-good reference seed\n   - all **121/121** Leiden result grids: **bit-identical labels**\n   - winning result and bin output: identical\n\n   That run yields 0 bins for *both* commits, which is a pre-existing property of that fixture and not the fix: the whole assembly is 3.5 Mbp, so no Leiden cluster reaches `MINIMUM_FINAL_BIN_SIZE` (200 kb) — the largest is 124 kb. Larger fixtures are unaffected (`cami3_v11_20260926_rerun`: 492 bins).\n\n### Still open (not mine to close)\n`41606c8` is currently **local only** — `origin/comebin-optimizations-v11` is still at `95f5ea8`, and `origin/master` is at `1b476a4`. The branch is now a clean 2-commit fast-forward ahead of `master` with no divergence, so the **merge to `master` + bioconda release prep is the remaining step**, as promised on #27. Flagging it here so it is not lost: the fix is not yet on GitHub.\n\nOne note left deliberately unaddressed to keep the blast radius small: the `OSError: [Errno 16] Device or resource busy: .../pymp-*` DataLoader temp-dir tracebacks in your log. They are non-fatal — training continued to epoch 200 — and are a separate cleanup problem, not part of this fix.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:03:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/28#issuecomment-5870418121","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXel9_w","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"I would like to have this fix and the working optimization merged together and(after all has been tested on the medium dataset in master asap","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:11:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/28#issuecomment-5870550527","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":28,"title":"Fix this issue","updatedAt":"2026-09-28T13:11:47Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/28"}  --- issue #25 details --- {"body":"Run at least 20 runs with different params or commits on the medium dataset and take the best based on bin stats and if similar based on runtime before running on larger data. Only take cami ii and iii human for the larger data from now on - archive the other benchmark data in zenodo and remove to get disc space, make use of the cami infrastructure, use amber for performace of cami II, use the gold standart if available, do not trim the data if full assembly is there, learn to export binning results as biobox format - cami standard, also export each binning result, bins in fasta, biobox output, stats as csv to zenodo","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXGzd7g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Thank you for the optimization ideas. I'm currently working on fix batches for COMEBin (see the optimization strategy in docs/09). Each fix batch is tested with the benchmark workflow (small → medium → large) before integration. What specific optimization areas are you most interested in? Current candidates include k-mer counting, coverage computation, clustering performance, and Leiden parameter sweeps.","createdAt":"2026-09-26T10:49:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/25#issuecomment-5845605870","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXHdDEw","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Optimization batch workflow confirmed: small → medium → large validation before integration, per docs/09-optimization-strategy.md. Current fix batches address: sequential bin numbering, float64 coverage depth consistency, sklearn KMeans compatibility, DataLoader drop_last edge case, and RNG seed reproducibility. Next candidates from code review: vectorized k-mer counting, closed-form covariance computation, set-based membership scans, and Leiden pool pruning (120 unseeded runs). Measuring per-stage wall time and peak RAM will guide priority ordering.","createdAt":"2026-09-26T12:31:03Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/25#issuecomment-5846287123","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXeb3dQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Optimization sweep — designed (plan + harness ready, launch pending run slot) ✅\n\nCommit `596a5536`:\n\n**Plan:** [docs/13-optimization-sweep-medium.md](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/docs/13-optimization-sweep-medium.md)\n- **24 runs** on the medium dataset (3,000 contigs, ~39 min each, seed 42): one-factor-at-a-time around the reference params (temperature, embedding sizes, batch size, HNSW max_edges, n_views, Leiden workers, HMM evalue) + 3 commit pins (master `904f649`, current v11 `95f5ea8`, the #28-fix `41606c8`) + 2 combos + seed sanity.\n- **Ranking**: bin stats first (CheckM2 comp/cont + HQ/MQ + F1, CheckM v1 cross-check), runtime as tiebreak — exactly as you asked.\n- **Then larger data = CAMI II & III human only**; demo/marine/medium/small/tiny archived to Zenodo and removed locally to free disk.\n- **AMBER** against the CAMI II gold standard (needs `setup.tar.gz`/GT import — flagged in docs/01) and no trimming of full assemblies.\n- **Biobox export**: new `scripts/export_biobox.sh` produces the CAMI-standard tarball (engine/version/binning/<sample>/<bin_id>.fna + binning_summary.tsv), concat bins.fasta.gz and a per-bin stats snapshot — validated on `medium_v11_20260924` (16 bins → 4.1 MB tarball).\n\n**Harness:** `scripts/run_comebin_fix.sh` now forwards optional params (TEMP / EMB / EMB_COV / BATCH / MAX_EDGES / LEIDEN_WORKERS / HMM_EVALUE) only when the invoked `run_comebin.sh` supports them, and records them in run_meta.\n\n⚠️ Launch is **blocked** until the current registered run (`small_v11_prepatch_baseline`) finishes — the harness refuses to overlap registered runs, per policy. Will launch the sweep as soon as the slot is free.","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:01:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/25#issuecomment-5870385013","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXemB3Q","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"**Sweep is live** (2026-09-28 13:12 UTC) — the 24-cell medium grid is running.\n\n- Driver: [`scripts/run_sweep_medium.sh`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/scripts/run_sweep_medium.sh) — detached, resumable (skips done cells, evals orphaned ones), never overlaps the registered run slot, one cell at a time.\n- Sources: v11 @ `95f5ea8` (reference base, matches `medium_v11_20260924`), unmodified upstream master @ `904f649` (unseeded, as in the original baselines), v11 @ `41606c8` (issue #28 fix → doubles as a no-regression check).\n- Params: THREADS=8, seed 42 (cell 24 = seed 7 reproducibility check), one-factor-at-a-time on temp / emb / embcov / batch / max_edges / n_views / leiden_workers / hmm_evalue + 2 combos. Cell 23 adjusted: early-stop is hardcoded in `run_comebin.sh` (not a CLI flag), so it's `emb_cov 512 + batch 512` instead of `noearly`.\n- Harness: added `N_VIEWS` forwarding + a `set -u` fix; every sweep flag is gated on the source's flag support, so neither the old master nor the v11 base is disturbed.\n\nCell 1 `sweep_001_ref` is in training (epoch ~few/200). Progress log: `status/sweep_medium.log`; I'll rank the finished cells by bin stats (CheckM2 completeness/contamination, HQ/MQ) then runtime when the grid completes.","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:11:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/25#issuecomment-5870551517","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":25,"title":"Improve optimization","updatedAt":"2026-09-28T13:11:51Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/25"}  --- issue #24 details --- {"body":"The readme is too full and should be for humans I want these sections\n- a:  the agent tag\n- b: a short summary what this project is we only focus on comebin from now on, aim to be best binner\nC: Progress:\n-  one bullet point latest acheivement\n- one bullet point what is the next step\n- d: then the 4 benchmark plots\n- e: then the all run table as requested \n- f: links to improtant parts of the project: zenodo, comebinfork, progress, all runs","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXGzd7w","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Thank you for the clean-up needed on the main README. I'll review the current README structure and ensure it reflects the latest run states, evaluation results, and benchmark status. The README currently has Current/Next sections, run history, and optimization strategy documentation that should stay in sync.","createdAt":"2026-09-26T10:49:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/24#issuecomment-5845605871","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXHdFiA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"README cleanup in progress. Current structure has Current/Next run sections, run history table, optimization strategy docs, and 4 benchmark plots (demo/human/marine/CAMI III). The run history at results/main_runs_table.md tracks 14+ runs with dataset, threads, commit, branch, bins, CheckM2/HQ/MQ, wall time, and exit code. Consider consolidating the 4 dataset-specific plots into a vertical arrangement per issue #19, and ensuring the 'Current/Next' banner reflects the latest completed run (cami3_v11_20260926_rerun: 492 bins, Zenodo v3 DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22973575).","createdAt":"2026-09-26T12:31:09Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/24#issuecomment-5846287752","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXeaatQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Delivered — README restructured into exactly the sections you asked ✅\n\nCommit `5cc93218`, README now has the short human-facing structure:\n\n- **a. Agent tag** — live status banner (heartbeat-updated) + activity/major-steps logs\n- **b. What this project is** — focus only on COMEBin from now on, aim: best binner\n- **c. Progress** — one bullet latest achievement, one bullet next step\n- **d. Benchmark plots** — the 4 datasets, stacked below each other\n- **e. All runs** — the full summary table (see #22)\n- **f. Important links** — Zenodo, COMEBin fork, PROGRESS, all runs, major-steps log\n\nThe long per-run prose moved out; the full history stays in [docs/11-run-results.md](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/docs/11-run-results.md).","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:00:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/24#issuecomment-5870361269","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXejHjA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"cool, remove the a,b,c keep the heading though","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:08:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/24#issuecomment-5870503820","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":24,"title":"Main readme needs cleaning","updatedAt":"2026-09-28T13:08:59Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/24"}  --- issue #19 details --- {"body":"show those https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/figures/combined_bar_plot.png below each other, and every commit/branch that is chosen for evaluation should be used on each of the benchmarks, so one can compare between updates","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXF4pvQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"make it 4 and add cami3 as the fourth, to make sure each dataset comparison should be a seperate plot and all 4 should be shown below each other","createdAt":"2026-09-26T08:34:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/19#issuecomment-5844642237","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXF_E3g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"The combined bar plot () already shows 2 rows (completeness <5%/<10%) × 3 columns (demo/human/marine) with run+branch labeling. For 'show those below each other': the current layout places them side-by-side. A vertical stack would improve comparability across datasets. Also, the per-dataset subplots in  could be extended to show all runs for a dataset. I'll add a vertical-arrangement option and update the README rendering.","createdAt":"2026-09-26T08:51:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/19#issuecomment-5844747486","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXHdTKA","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Combined bar plot (results/figures/combined_bar_plot.png) already shows 2 rows (completeness <5%/<10%) × 3 columns (demo/human/marine) with run+branch labeling. For 'show those below each other': a vertical arrangement would improve dataset comparability. The per-dataset subplots in docs/09 could be extended to show all runs for each dataset vertically. I'll add a vertical-arrangement option and update the README rendering. CAMI III as fourth dataset would complete the set (currently demo 29,434 / human 4,900 / marine 41,988 contigs).","createdAt":"2026-09-26T12:31:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/19#issuecomment-5846291240","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXeaXfg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Delivered — 4 datasets, plotted below each other ✅\n\nCommit `5cc93218`: `scripts/make_combined_bar_plot.py` now plots **four** datasets — demo / CAMI II human / CAMI II marine / **CAMI III toy human gut** — with **one row per dataset, all rows stacked below each other** (4 rows × 2 contamination-cutoff columns: <5 % and <10 %). Every evaluated run of that dataset is its own stacked bar labelled `run · commit · branch`, so a commit/branch evaluated on multiple datasets shows up on each of them and is directly comparable between updates.\n\nRendered: [results/figures/combined_bar_plot.png](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/figures/combined_bar_plot.png) (also .svg). Run matrix: [results/main_runs_table.md](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/main_runs_table.md) — 5 rows incl. cami3 (492 bins).","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:00:03Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/19#issuecomment-5870360446","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXehTvg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"make the plot a bit nicer and readable, the text on the y axis is too long","createdAt":"2026-09-28T13:07:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/19#issuecomment-5870474174","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":19,"title":"better plots","updatedAt":"2026-09-28T13:07:13Z","url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/19"}


